---
/**
 * Terms of Service.
 *
 * The second half of audit finding C3. Also does real commercial work: it sets
 * out the coaching-not-therapy boundary that appears throughout the site, and
 * states the cancellation and refund position for a $3,600 programme before
 * anyone pays for one.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import { graph, breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/seo';

const title = 'Terms of Service | Harrison Saito';
const description =
  'Terms governing coaching, mentoring and tutoring services provided by Harrison Saito, including scope, fees, cancellation and the limits of coaching.';

const updated = '5 August 2026';

const schema = graph(
  breadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Terms of Service', url: '/terms' },
  ])
);
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/terms" schema={schema}>
  <section class="section legal-hero section--deep">
    <div class="container container--narrow" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="display-l">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="legal-hero__meta">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow legal" data-reveal>
      <p class="legal__intro">
        These terms govern your use of this website and any coaching, mentoring or tutoring services
        provided by Harrison Saito. By using this site or engaging my services, you agree to them.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Nature of the services — please read this one</h2>
      <p>
        I provide <strong>coaching, mentoring and tutoring</strong>. I am not a psychologist,
        psychiatrist, counsellor, social worker or medical practitioner, and nothing I provide is
        psychological treatment, medical advice, diagnosis, or emergency care.
      </p>
      <p>
        Coaching is a training framework for the inner world. It draws on martial arts, Buddhist
        philosophy and structured self-inquiry. It is not a substitute for treatment of a mental
        health condition. If you have or suspect you have a mental health condition, please consult a
        registered health practitioner. I may decline or end an engagement where I believe clinical
        support would serve you better, and I will say so directly.
      </p>
      <p class="legal__alert">
        If you are in crisis or at risk of harm, contact Lifeline on
        <a href="tel:131114">13 11 14</a>, the Suicide Call Back Service on
        <a href="tel:1300659467">1300 659 467</a>, or call <a href="tel:000">000</a> immediately.
        Do not use this website's forms for urgent matters — they are not monitored continuously.
      </p>

      <h2>2. No guarantee of outcome</h2>
      <p>
        Coaching and tutoring outcomes depend substantially on your own effort, honesty and
        circumstances. I do not guarantee any particular result, including any ATAR, mark, rank,
        income, relationship or emotional outcome. Testimonials on this site describe individual
        experiences and are not a promise of similar results.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Engagement, fees and payment</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Fees published on this site are in Australian dollars and include GST where applicable.</li>
        <li>
          Session-based coaching and mentoring are payable per session unless otherwise agreed in
          writing.
        </li>
        <li>
          The <em>Return to Self</em> programme is a 12-week engagement. Payment terms, including any
          instalment arrangement, are agreed in writing before the programme begins.
        </li>
        <li>
          Submitting an application or enquiry does not create a binding engagement. An engagement
          begins when I confirm it and you accept the agreed terms.
        </li>
        <li>I may change published fees at any time; changes do not affect an engagement already agreed.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Cancellation and rescheduling</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Individual sessions may be rescheduled with at least 24 hours' notice at no charge.
          Sessions cancelled with less notice, or missed, may be charged in full.
        </li>
        <li>
          For the 12-week programme, you may withdraw at any time. Fees for sessions already
          delivered are non-refundable. Any refund of the unused balance is at my discretion and will
          be dealt with reasonably and in good faith.
        </li>
        <li>
          If I need to cancel or reschedule, I will offer an alternative time or refund the affected
          portion.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Confidentiality</h2>
      <p>
        What you tell me in a session stays between us. I will not disclose it without your consent,
        except where disclosure is required by law, or where I hold a reasonable belief that
        disclosure is necessary to prevent a serious and imminent threat to the life, health or
        safety of any person.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Students under 18</h2>
      <p>
        Where a student is under 18, a parent or guardian must arrange the engagement and is
        responsible for fees. I may share general progress with the parent or guardian. I hold a
        current Working With Children Check, which can be provided on request.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your responsibilities</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide accurate information about your circumstances and any relevant health matters.</li>
        <li>Attend sessions on time and engage in good faith.</li>
        <li>Take responsibility for your own decisions and actions arising from our work.</li>
        <li>Seek appropriate professional support where a matter falls outside coaching.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        All content on this website — text, images, video, programme structure and materials — is
        owned by Harrison Saito or used with permission, and is protected by copyright. Materials
        provided to you during an engagement are for your personal use and may not be reproduced,
        distributed or resold without written permission.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Liability</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing in these terms excludes, restricts or modifies any guarantee, right or remedy you
        have under the Australian Consumer Law that cannot lawfully be excluded. Where liability can
        be limited, my liability is limited to resupplying the services or paying the cost of having
        them resupplied.
      </p>
      <p>
        To the extent permitted by law, I am not liable for indirect or consequential loss arising
        from your use of this website or the services.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Website use</h2>
      <p>
        This website is provided on an "as is" basis. I may change or withdraw content at any time.
        Links to third-party sites are provided for convenience and do not imply endorsement or
        responsibility for their content.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Personal information is handled in accordance with the
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, which forms part of these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of New South Wales, Australia. The courts of New South
        Wales have non-exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Harrison Saito<br />
        {SITE.locality}, {SITE.region}, Australia<br />
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a><br />
        <a href={`tel:${SITE.phone}`}>{SITE.phoneDisplay}</a>
      </p>

      <aside class="legal__note">
        <p>
          These terms have been drafted to reflect how this business actually operates. They are not
          legal advice. Have them reviewed by an Australian legal practitioner before relying on
          them — particularly clauses 3, 4 and 9, which carry commercial risk.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal-hero { padding-block: clamp(7rem, 15vh, 10rem) clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem); }
  .legal-hero__meta {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-on-ink-faint);
  }

  .legal { max-width: 44rem; }

  .legal__intro {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-on-paper);
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .legal h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }

  .legal p { margin-bottom: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-on-paper-muted); }

  .legal ul {
    margin: 0 0 1.35rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }
  .legal li { line-height: 1.75; color: var(--text-on-paper-muted); }
  .legal li::marker { color: var(--gold-deep); }

  .legal a { color: var(--gold-deep); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }

  .legal__alert {
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    background: oklch(52% 0.19 27 / 0.06);
    border-left: 2px solid oklch(52% 0.19 27);
    color: var(--text-on-paper) !important;
  }

  .legal__note {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding: 1.35rem 1.5rem;
    background: var(--paper-warm);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--gold);
  }
  .legal__note p { margin: 0; font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--text-on-paper-muted); }
</style>
